### Test Add Questions From Bank to Exam API

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@teacherEmail = teacher@example.com
@teacherPassword = password123
# Note: You may need to update the token or login credentials

### 1. Login as Teacher (Optional - to get token)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{teacherEmail}}",
  "password": "{{teacherPassword}}"
}

### Variable for Token
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 2. Create a Lecture Exam (if needed)
# Assumes lectureId 1 exists and belongs to teacher
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lectureId": 1,
  "title": "Test Exam with Bank Questions",
  "totalGrade": 100,
  "duration": 60,
  "isVisible": true
}

### Variable for Exam ID
@examId = 1
# Update locally if needed, or use {{createExam.response.body.exam.id}} if supported by your runner

### 3. Add Questions from Bank
# Assumes question IDs 1 and 2 exist in the question bank
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exams/{{examId}}/questions/from-bank
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "questionIds": [1, 2]
}

### 4. Verify Questions Added
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exams/{{examId}}/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
